      "### Project Overview\n",
      "\n",
      "- **Purpose**: A classic Tetris clone written in C++.\n",
      "- **Graphics & Audio**: Uses the **raylib** library for rendering and sound playback.\n",
      "- **Core Components**  \n",
      "  - `block.h / block.cpp`: Defines individual tetromino blocks and their rotations.  \n",
      "  - `blocks.cpp`: Provides the set of all seven tetromino shapes.  \n",
      "  - `grid.h / grid.cpp`: Manages the playfield grid, line clearing, and collision detection.  \n",
      "  - `game.h / game.cpp`: Implements the main game loop, input handling, scoring, and state transitions.  \n",
      "  - `position.h / position.cpp`: Utility for 2D coordinates used throughout the game.  \n",
      "  - `colors.h / colors.cpp`: Stores color definitions for each tetromino type.  \n",
      "  - `main.cpp`: Entry point that initializes raylib, loads assets, and starts the game loop.  \n",
      "- **Assets**  \n",
      "  - Font (`monogram.ttf`) for UI text.  \n",
      "  - Sound files (`clear.mp3`, `music.mp3`, `rotate.mp3`) for gameplay feedback.  \n",
      "- **Build**: A `Makefile` is provided to compile the project on supported platforms.  \n",
      "- **Documentation**: `README.md` contains usage instructions and a brief description of the game.  \n",
      "\n",
